## Modifier Rotation Rules (3D Structural Matrix)

Each Voynich modifier applies a deterministic rotation to the ROOT vector.

### Modifier Classes
- Soft modifiers (vowel-like): X-axis rotation, 5°–15°
- Hard modifiers (consonant-like): Y-axis rotation, 15°–35°
- Currier-B modifiers: Z-axis rotation, 35°–75°

### Transformation Rule
V' = Rz(θz) · Ry(θy) · Rx(θx) · V

Where:
- V is the ROOT vector
- θx, θy, θz are rotation angles determined by modifier class
- Rx, Ry, Rz are standard rotation matrices

### Compound Modifiers
Multiple modifiers apply sequential rotations in the order they appear.

### Cadence
Cadence tokens (daiin, aiin, dy, am, al) determine radial distance from origin.

### Plant-Segment Boundary
`<-><!plant>` resets momentum but not position.
